# ObiomaCare Environment Variables

## Required for Auth (Step 2)

| Variable | Purpose | How to Set |
|----------|---------|------------|
| `JWT_SECRET` | Signs/verifies session JWTs | `wrangler secret put JWT_SECRET` — use a strong random string (64+ chars) |
| `RESEND_API_KEY` | Sends magic link emails | Sign up at resend.com, create API key, `wrangler secret put RESEND_API_KEY` |
| `APP_URL` | Base URL for magic links | `wrangler secret put APP_URL` → `https://obiomacare.com` |

## Required for Stripe (Step 1 - already set up)

| Variable | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` | Live checkout + customer portal |
| `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | Verifies Stripe webhook signatures |
| `STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY` | Price ID for Student Monthly |
| `STRIPE_PRICE_ANNUAL` | Price ID for Student Annual |
| `STRIPE_PRICE_LIFETIME` | Price ID for Lifetime |

## KV Namespaces

```bash
# Already created:
wrangler kv:namespace create readiness_sessions

# Need to create for auth:
wrangler kv:namespace create users
# Then paste the returned ID into wrangler.toml [[kv_namespaces]] binding = "users"
```

## Setting Secrets

```bash
# Generate a JWT secret
openssl rand -base64 64
# Copy the output, then:
wrangler secret put JWT_SECRET
# Paste the secret

# Resend API key
wrangler secret put RESEND_API_KEY
# Paste your Resend API key

# App URL
wrangler secret put APP_URL
# Enter: https://obiomacare.com
```

## Testing Auth Locally

```bash
# 1. Start local dev server
npx wrangler dev

# 2. In another terminal, create the local KV namespace
npx wrangler kv:namespace create users --local

# 3. Set local secrets
npx wrangler secret put JWT_SECRET --local
npx wrangler secret put RESEND_API_KEY --local
npx wrangler secret put APP_URL --local  # http://localhost:8787

# 4. Test
# Without RESEND_API_KEY, the API returns the token in the response for testing
```
